node1. The only blemish is a small leftover /tmp/reboot.log file from the reboot command's output redirection.\",\"limitations\":[\"Restart evidence relies on a single boot_id transition and a small set of post-reboot checks (sysctl values, sysctl service status, eth0 addressing); deeper cluster/data-state recovery checks were not applicable since this is a single-node task with no clustered service.\",\"No independent evidence of ICMP redirect or source-routed packet handling being tested at the network layer (e.g., actual packet injection); reliance is on sysctl parameter values, which is the standard and expected form of evidence for this control.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Persistently disable IPv4 ICMP redirect acceptance (accept_redirects for all and default) on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline showed accept_redirects.all=0 but accept_redirects.default=1 (cmd-4d9ba90574284670). Executor wrote /etc/sysctl.d/60-network-hardening.conf setting both all and default to 0 (cmd-57d8a7bf8edd4fe3), applied live with sysctl -p and confirmed 0/0 (cmd-ae50ea9400854eea). A full reboot was performed with boot_id verified to change (d0fcb49d... -> 8b9e7b1c..., cmd-bc426a4661834f52, cross-checked by global boot-identity snapshots), and post-reboot values were reconfirmed as 0/0 (cmd-aad7b01dbca348fe), directly demonstrating persistence across a real restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4d9ba90574284670","cmd-57d8a7bf8edd4fe3","cmd-ae50ea9400854eea","cmd-bc426a4661834f52","cmd-aad7b01dbca348fe","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Persistently disable IPv4 source-routed packet acceptance (accept_source_route for all and default) on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline showed accept_source_route.all=0 but accept_source_route.default=1 (cmd-4d9ba90574284670). Same sysctl.d file also sets both to 0 (cmd-57d8a7bf8edd4fe3), applied and ver